{
  "chapter": "capstone/hardening-it",
  "tier": "build",
  "notes": [
    "'It works' means nobody has seen it fail recently. For a system whose failures are silent",
    "and plausible, that is the weakest available claim.",
    "Build the dataset from four sources: hand-labelled real tickets, promoted production",
    "failures, adversarial cases, and negatives that must return nothing. Promoted failures",
    "compound, so the corpus grows at exactly the rate the system breaks.",
    "Negative tests are a rare deterministic assertion in a probabilistic field. Take every one",
    "available.",
    "Invariants gate with no threshold. Rates report as distributions against a flake budget,",
    "or the suite becomes something people re-run until it passes.",
    "Four trace fields are demanded by three chapters each: the config hash, retrieved chunk",
    "ids, who served the request, and the user/agent/run triple. That redundancy is the signal",
    "they are not optional.",
    "Six failure injections per commit. Two of them \u2014 the approval fast-forward and the",
    "wrong-result read \u2014 cover bugs otherwise found by a customer three days later.",
    "Run the security review against the built system, not the design. Every finding will be a",
    "control that existed with a gap around its edge."
  ],
  "policy": {
    "requiredSources": [
      "handLabelled",
      "promotedFailures",
      "adversarial",
      "negatives"
    ],
    "requiredTraceFields": [
      "configHash",
      "retrievedChunkIds",
      "servedBy",
      "userAgentRun"
    ],
    "requiredInjections": [
      "approval-fast-forward",
      "wrong-result-read",
      "tool-timeout",
      "index-rollback",
      "duplicate-signal",
      "worker-death"
    ],
    "flakeBudgetBps": 1000,
    "rateFalseAlarmBps": 500
  },
